{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to factor the quadratic expression \\(6y^2 - y - 51\\) into the form \\((3Ay + B)(y - C)\\). We start by expanding the form \\((3Ay + B)(y - C)\\):\n\n\\[\n(3Ay + B)(y - C) = 3Ay^2 + By - 3ACy - BC = 3Ay^2 + (B - 3AC)y - BC\n\\]\n\nWe need to match this with the original quadratic expression \\(6y^2 - y - 51\\). By comparing coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n1. \\(3A = 6\\)\n2. \\(B - 3AC = -1\\)\n3. \\(-BC = -51\\)\n\nFrom the first equation, we solve for \\(A\\):\n\n\\[\n3A = 6 \\implies A = 2\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(A = 2\\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\nB - 3(2)C = -1 \\implies B - 6C = -1 \\implies B = 6C - 1\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(A = 2\\) and \\(B = 6C - 1\\) into the third equation:\n\n\\[\n-BC = -51 \\implies B = \\frac{51}{C}\n\\]\n\nSince \\(B = 6C - 1\\) and \\(B = \\frac{51}{C}\\), we can set these two expressions for \\(B\\) equal to each other:\n\n\\[\n6C - 1 = \\frac{51}{C}\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":897,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8168,279,79151,7493,17767,21,88,61,17,481,379,481,220,20,16,57758,1119,279,1352,1124,1188,18,73109,488,425,2376,88,481,356,10699,568,1205,1191,553,23175,279,1352,1124,1188,18,73109,488,425,2376,88,481,356,10699,7731,59,9640,7,18,73109,488,425,2376,88,481,356,8,284,220,18,73109,61,17,488,3216,481,220,18,1706,88,481,18040,284,220,18,73109,61,17,488,320,33,481,220,18,1706,83347,481,18040,198,59,2533,1654,1184,311,2432,419,448,279,4024,79151,7493,17767,21,88,61,17,481,379,481,220,20,16,59,568,3216,26297,36829,11,582,633,279,2701,1849,315,37906,1447,16,13,17767,18,32,284,220,21,59,340,17,13,17767,33,481,220,18,1706,284,481,16,59,340,18,13,1124,4080,4897,284,481,20,16,59,692,3830,279,1156,23606,11,582,11625,369,17767,32,59,7731,59,9640,18,32,284,220,21,1124,6383,550,362,